    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Grammarly is a for-profit company founded in 2009 and headquartered in San Francisco, CA. Its core offering is an AI writing assistant that provides suggestions for grammar, tone, and text generation across applications and websites. The company describes itself as making AI writing convenient through personalized guidance, and it states that it does not sell or monetize user content, provide it for advertising purposes, or allow third-party service providers to train their models on user content.\n\nThe company tracks two primary products: Grammarly, a general writing and editing tool that reads document text broadly, and Grammarly for Education, an institutional product that includes generative AI features, student data handling, and FERPA compliance considerations. The company claims that organizations deploying Grammarly save an average of $5,000 per employee per year, and references a figure of 17x in connection with that claim. It also references a product called Superhuman Go, described as delivering writing support alongside productivity agents.\n\nNo litigation, MCP server registrations, or SEC or patent filings appear in the held facts for this company.",
